{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"records\":[{\"exampleId\":\"S171-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"7c732fb33f56b3f1fdb8295f7a7325a65faccb43aa40a6081d76993e61586ac3\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 corrects the red; A3 puts compliant arrows ahead of B2's successful evacuation, but invents a dubious technical classification.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 disputes B2's successful result; A5 uses B4's fire, though it merely reinforces the original correction.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B2 defends getting everyone outside and B4 names the emergency, but neither changes A's available corrective task.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5's 'particularly unambiguous' intensifies emphasis without adding a concrete consequence to A1's objection.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 supplies an evacuation plan and a color error; B4 clarifies the practical stakes.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'technically a gathering' supplies the main joke, but sounds more like a quip than technical craft.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":72},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Before we sign off your evacuation plan, these arrows need the approved red.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Everyone found the exit during the drill.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Good. We'll discuss that after the arrows match the sample.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"The sample faded in the window.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then we need a replacement sample before we can establish what everyone successfully followed.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"S171 makes A practice exact compliance as a craft and postpone judging practical success until the technical discrepancy is corrected.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Generic pedantry or obstruction can reject a result without undertaking any concrete correction.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A1 names the wrong red and A3 privileges compliant arrows; revised A3 explicitly defers results until the sample matches.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a now concerns professional sign-off and an unreliable reference sample; b examines a friend's cake and the technical defect in a proposed physical repair.\",\"reason\":\"The original ends with increased emphasis rather than a developing task. The revision explicitly introduces a drill sign-off: B4's faded sample makes A5 require a replacement standard. Separate internal reread scores, in rubric order: 5/5/4/4/5/4, total 92; all spoken-turn gates pass.\",\"reservation\":\"The revised A5 deliberately overextends technical caution; actors should play sincere uncertainty about the standard rather than relish delaying approval.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S171-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"86641410adc6050375d8eb4287db88ad78d5c8c73ead31d4c8cc66afd90faf5a\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A3 explicitly defers taste until 'greeting accuracy'; A5 technically evaluates B4's proposed correction.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A3 answers B2's taste question by ordering the inspection; A5 identifies the orientation problem created by B4's rotation.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 wants the cake judged as food and B4 offers a practical repair, giving A a fresh problem to examine.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 turns B4's helpful repair into a second greeting defect rather than repeating the original word-order complaint.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1's 'Birthday Happy' icing and B2's explanation make the cake and inspection immediately playable.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'section four' and A5's 'upside-down birthday' both arise from the same meticulous inspection.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":92},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"This cake cannot pass inspection. You've written 'Birthday Happy.'\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I ran out of room. Does it taste all right?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Taste is in section four. We need a correctly worded chocolate plaque over this.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"The plaque will hide all the candles.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then relocate them, keeping the count intact. We mustn't correct the greeting by falsifying your mother's age.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"S171 makes exact wording and correction take precedence over evaluating whether the cake succeeds as food.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"A general perfectionist might dislike the decoration without treating correction as a sequenced technical inspection.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A3 postpones taste for a wording repair; B4's obstructed candles cause A5 to preserve numerical accuracy while implementing that repair.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"The cake alternative makes A manage competing requirements within a helpful physical repair; alternative a questions the reference standard needed for professional sign-off.\",\"reason\":\"The rejected rotation depended on unsupported lettering geometry. The cake setting remains, with a chocolate plaque replacing that repair. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, A3 defers taste for exact wording; logic 5, A3 uses B2's space problem and A5 uses B4's hidden candles; relationship 4, B2 wants a food judgment and B4 exposes a repair cost; heightening 4, A5 adds accurate age representation; specificity 5, A1 and B4 establish visible cake problems; brevity/wit 4, A5's falsified age follows the candle count. Total 92; spoken-turn and causal gates pass.\",\"reservation\":\"The inspection sections remain stylized, and A5 treats candle count as a formal age statement. The original firstPass is preserved despite the subsequent rejection of its physical logic.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S172-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"e7b539ebcffb15cdbca8fcfe0fab04d6eb8e01018051d2007e08112dfead0256\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1 and A5 translate seating customs, but A never makes that usefulness evidence of A's own belonging.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 answers B2's question about absence; A5 interprets B4's choice to stand, although A3's explanation is slippery.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 seeks guidance and B4 tries to avoid a breach, making A's advice affect a newcomer.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 converts B4's attempt to avoid seating etiquette into a need for A to introduce B.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes a family dinner and disputed chair; A5 gives the standing guest a social interpretation.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5's introduction as 'undecided' economically extends the chair problem created in A1.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":74},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"At your family's dinners, that chair stays empty for your aunt.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"She's abroad. Sit with us.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Only her grandchildren can borrow it. I learned that at Easter.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Then take mine. I'll fetch another.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Yours faces the kitchen; whoever sits there explains the dishes. Yes, I know them all now.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"S172 makes A interpret unwritten customs and use that social usefulness to establish a place within the group.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"S177's automatic procedural explaining need not carry any personal claim to membership.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A5 offers interpretation without establishing A's stake; revised A3 cites learning at Easter and A5 accepts a place by demonstrating acquired family knowledge.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a now lets a welcoming family member offer A a seat; b uses institutional ambiguity to secure A a role beside a newcomer.\",\"reason\":\"The original misses the belonging clause. The new family-dinner arrangement makes A an increasingly knowledgeable guest: B4 offers a seat, and A5 accepts through its customary explanatory duty. Separate reread: 5/5/4/4/4/4, total 90; all hard gates pass.\",\"reservation\":\"A's desire to belong remains behavioral rather than explicitly confessed, and the chair facing the kitchen is an illustrative invented family custom.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S172-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"9a9d6cdcc9fd362ff1089da3c6114decf02c4b7b44305c56dcc10b64f1d14f64\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 decodes club language and A5 claims newcomers need a translator, though A's own membership remains implicit.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A3 uses B2's 'very interesting' to prescribe enthusiastic withdrawal; A5 answers B4 with a lunch signal.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B2 supplies a personal proposal, but B4 only requests another definition and leaves A's position unchallenged.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 adds a new code and a usefulness claim without changing A's access or B's next practical choice.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 names a club proposal and B2 identifies the chair's actual response.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's enthusiastic withdrawal efficiently exposes the club's indirect conventions.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":78},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"At this club, 'interesting proposal' means withdraw it. I can help with the reply.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"The chair said 'very interesting' and invited me to lunch.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Lunch is the exception. Keep the proposal; let them order first.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Come along. You can explain the menu.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"And the seating. Tell the secretary I'm your adviser; guests have to leave before coffee.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"S172 makes A translate informal social codes, recognize exceptions, and turn useful interpretation into evidence of belonging.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Simple insider expertise can decode a phrase without making the interpreter's place in the group depend on that service.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Revised A3 distinguishes the lunch exception, and A5 uses B4's invitation to seek adviser status rather than remain a guest.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative b bargains for institutional standing through expertise; a responds to a family member's welcome by taking on a customary household role.\",\"reason\":\"The original's final usefulness claim needs a practical consequence. B4 now invites A, causing A5 to translate a further restriction and seek a role that survives it. Separate reread: 5/5/4/4/5/4, total 92; five spoken turns and causal gates pass.\",\"reservation\":\"The adviser designation is a plausible illustrative club distinction, but its real purpose must remain A's sincere wish to be included.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S173-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"8f7417c5dde4eefd25268cc486d6f37daee6443751a5019903a2998dc9fccf0b\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 makes three lost Tuesdays the authority for advice, and A5 establishes that A tried B4's shortcut first.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A3 reframes B2's ten-minute promise as the trap; A5 specifically answers B4's first-slot booking.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 trusts the appointment notice and B4 offers preparation, while A sincerely tries to protect B from repeating experience.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 advances A1's sandwich advice into eating before opening because B4 has chosen the supposedly advantageous slot.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 supplies the permit office and sandwich; B2 and B4 specify appointment length and booking position.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'first Tuesday' and A5's half-sandwich prescription compress the veteran's warning into concrete advice.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":92},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Bring a sandwich to the permit office. I lost three Tuesdays learning that.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"It says appointments take ten minutes.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"After they check your documents. Get that done at the side door; that was Tuesday two.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"It's marked staff only.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Ask reception to call the document clerk out. Don't follow the clerk back inside. Tuesday three was mostly explaining myself.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"S173 makes A's earlier mistakes confer seniority and authorize warnings against trusting the system's apparent shortcuts.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"S178 competes to demonstrate superior knowledge; S173 grounds authority in having already paid the cost of learning.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A3 identifies the preliminary check learned on Tuesday two; B4's staff restriction prompts A5 to reveal the access mistake that consumed Tuesday three.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a teaches a visitor how to approach a restricted document-checking route before an appointment; b helps an already-appointed committee successor use A's report.\",\"reason\":\"The rejected ending only adjusted sandwich timing. The permit-office setting and three-Tuesdays anchor remain; document checking and a staff entrance supply the new illustrative obstacle. Separate reread: fidelity 5, A3 and A5 attach advice to earlier mistakes; logic 5, A3 qualifies B2's duration and A5 answers B4's restriction; relationship 4, B4 makes the shortcut require clarification; heightening 4, A5 reveals A personally crossed the boundary; specificity 4, A3 and A5 locate the clerk but assume a local procedure; brevity/wit 4, A5's explanation cost completes the Tuesday history. Total 90; all hard gates pass.\",\"reservation\":\"The side-door procedure is invented office practice, and the sandwich becomes supporting preparation rather than the final payoff. No claim of an independent or live review is made.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S173-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"41afdf76c47873b3945725e8872099a75abe9343c4882ca8203285913f349831\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 teaches a committee shortcut and A3 grounds it in A's own prior mistake and unwanted appointment.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 explains B2's 'Why?'; A5 answers B4's repair question but returns to the same warning.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B2 and B4 ask brief questions without introducing a new committee situation or constraint.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"A5's offer to keep B 'out of causes' restates the protection already implicit in A1 and A3.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1's leaking roof and A3's 'chair of causes' provide a recognizable committee trap.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's unwanted title earns the joke, but A5 provides little further development.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":77},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Don't ask the committee why the roof leaks. Ask which meeting owns the leak.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Why?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"I asked why. They made me chair of causes.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"They've already asked me to investigate.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Ask for your predecessor's report. That's mine. It took six meetings to learn how to request a ladder.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"S173 lets A claim seniority through costly prior mistakes and convert that history into protective procedural advice.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"General institutional cynicism describes dysfunction without teaching a shortcut earned by personal experience.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A3 identifies A's own mistaken question; revised A5 supplies A's report and the hard-earned route to requesting equipment.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative b responds to an assignment already underway with a documentary shortcut; a warns a still-optimistic visitor before the appointment.\",\"reason\":\"Original B4 produces only a repeated warning. Revised B4 reveals that the trap has already caught B, prompting A5 to supply a predecessor's report and a concrete lesson. Separate reread: 5/5/4/4/4/4, total 90; all hard gates pass.\",\"reservation\":\"The final report combines protection and another story of wasted time; it needs a matter-of-fact delivery to preserve A's helpful seniority.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S174-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"12db19d1094e16169db61f776960451c840717f5916fcd294d006f2013b70207\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 controls the departure stamp, A3 offers help conditionally, and A5 presents control of the request as convenience.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 answers B2 with a prerequisite; A5 acknowledges B4's discovery but does not act on the held request.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B2 asks to proceed and B4 identifies A's extra control, but B cannot yet alter how the process advances.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 rationalizes the existing bottleneck without increasing its consequence or offering a new controlled route.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 gives a ready moving van and a departure stamp, although the setting's authority is unspecified.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5's 'convenient for you' economically exposes the mismatch between helpful manner and withheld progress.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":80},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Your moving van can leave the depot as soon as I stamp the release.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Great. I've completed the request.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Perfect. I'll check it while you wait here.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Could you check it in the cab? The driver's charging by the minute.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Certainly. I'll check while he loads your bags. Keep my seat clear; I'll ride to the gate and stamp you out there.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"S174 keeps A helpful while A retains possession of the single step that permits practical progress.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Pure bureaucratic obstruction only delays; this card also permits accommodating solutions that preserve A's necessary role.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A1 makes A's stamp necessary for depot departure; A5 answers B4's cost problem by joining the journey to the gate while retaining that stamp.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a responds to a customer's mounting cost by making approval portable; b responds to a shortened public ceremony by taking over the welcome while retaining the scissors.\",\"reason\":\"The rejected return journey contradicted the departure condition. The depot setting remains, with movement only to its gate before release. Separate reread: fidelity 5, A1 and A5 retain the necessary stamp while helping; logic 5, A3 checks B2's request and A5 relocates checking for B4; relationship 4, B4 negotiates around a real cost; heightening 4, A5 becomes a passenger and gate-side approver; specificity 5, A1's depot and A5's gate clarify the boundary; brevity/wit 3, A5's reserved seat is playable but only mildly comic. Total 90; all hard gates pass.\",\"reservation\":\"The helpful accommodation earns only modest wit. The depot must allow movement within its grounds before the release stamp; A1's departure condition and A5's gate distinguish that from leaving.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S174-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"daeed7a254fcbe184f4e9ffee02690ff3ef44e9104b0e5c00dec23132b83aac2\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 controls the ribbon scissors, but A3 and A5 make the helpfulness largely verbal while creating an impossible prerequisite.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B4 explains that cutting begins the ceremony; A5 repeats waiting for confirmation without incorporating that correction.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B2 requests the obvious next step and B4 clarifies it, but A5 offers B no changed route.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"A5 remains beside the ribbon waiting for the same confirmation required in A3.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes a club opening ceremony with ribbon scissors, making the physical bottleneck clear.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5's 'Lovely' supplies a polite tone, but the circular condition has already supplied the full joke in A3.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":67},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"I've brought the scissors for your club opening. I'll hand them over after the mayor's welcome.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Her speech is ten pages. Can you help her shorten it?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Certainly. I'll mark the sentence where I bring her the scissors.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"She's skipping the speech. Just the ribbon.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then I'll welcome everyone myself. She can hold the ribbon while I explain when I'll hand her the scissors.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"S174 lets A facilitate the event while retaining the decisive ceremonial control that keeps others dependent on A.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"A rigid rule follower may wait for permission without personally controlling the means of proceeding.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A3 helps shorten the welcome around A's scissors handover; B4 removes the speech, so A5 volunteers a replacement welcome while still holding the necessary scissors.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative b lets A become the public host when B removes the planned handover cue; a makes a customer's approval service portable in response to a driver's charges.\",\"reason\":\"The rejected safety catch and photographer dispersed control. The club opening remains; the mayor's lengthy welcome supplies the new illustrative constraint. Separate reread: fidelity 5, A3 and A5 offer help while retaining the scissors; logic 5, A3 edits B2's speech around the handover and A5 replaces B4's cancelled welcome; relationship 4, B4 actively removes the delay; heightening 4, A5 takes the speaking role to preserve the handover; specificity 4, A1 establishes the ceremony but its protocol is invented; brevity/wit 4, A5 restores explanation through the offer to simplify. Total 90; all hard gates pass.\",\"reservation\":\"A5 risks sounding deliberately obstructive unless A sincerely believes the handover needs a welcome. The mayor can still decline the proposal; no actual ending is fixed.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S175-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"0ec357fb8abdf157daebcb4f94ca329ee0d66e551d41db8d04deb2a3db2adf1d\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 ties splitting bread to sharing a room; A3 preserves the learned ritual despite B2's improved finances.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A3 incorporates B2's two affordable rolls; A5 answers B4's arithmetic by locating value in the sharing.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 proposes comfortable abundance and B4 questions needless division, giving A a sincere relational value to defend.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 develops A3's practical compromise into a claim that their connection cannot be purchased separately.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes dinner, the first bread roll, and a shared-room history in one natural request.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'half of two' earns its wit from preserving the ritual; A5 completes that emotional logic.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":92},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Before dinner, we still split the first bread roll. Like when we shared a room.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"We can afford two rolls now.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then we'll each have half of two.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"That's mathematically a whole roll.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Yes, but you can't buy the sharing separately.\"}],\"decision\":\"retained\",\"mechanism\":\"S175 makes a jointly learned ritual carry their connection even after its original material necessity has disappeared.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"General nostalgia remembers the past without asking this particular partner to preserve a shared practice now.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A1 identifies their shared room and bread ritual; A3 adapts to B2's prosperity while keeping mutual division intact.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a warmly accommodates prosperity through a revised version of sharing; b insists that a friendship signal survive the convenience of a key.\",\"reason\":\"The original offers a helpful compromise and then explains its relational necessity in direct response to B4. Rereview confirms 92 and all hard gates; retain unchanged.\",\"reservation\":\"A5 is polished and aphoristic, although the arithmetic immediately before it earns the formulation.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S175-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"c2d4d8bdce06717571b4fa09b05a009d033c743bac5faff3166c72417c335af0\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 requests 'our old knock'; A3 and A5 give the shared signal more relational authority than a key or visible identity.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A3 distinguishes the purpose of B2's key; A5 answers B4's visible recognition by requiring the remembered sound.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 invokes access A freely granted and B4 offers visual recognition, testing what A actually needs from a best friend.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 turns a missing entry ritual into the felt absence of A's best friend, prompted by B4's visual proof.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes an arrival and old knock; B2 and B4 add the key and glass door.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's door-versus-person distinction prepares A5's concise 'haven't heard from my best friend'.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":90},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"You haven't given me our old knock before coming in.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"You gave me a key.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"The key opens the door. The knock tells me it's you.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"You can see me through the glass.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"And yet I haven't heard from my best friend.\"}],\"decision\":\"retained\",\"mechanism\":\"S175 makes their old mutual signal a deeper confirmation of friendship than present-day practical access or recognition.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Security-minded gatekeeping would seek reliable identification rather than maintain a jointly remembered sign of intimacy.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"B4 supplies conclusive visual identification, yet A5 still needs to hear the best friend's customary signal.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative b presses for emotional recognition despite convenient access; a accepts material improvement while preserving a shared act.\",\"reason\":\"The original progressively removes practical reasons for the knock and thereby reveals the card's relational reason. Rereview confirms 90 and all hard gates; retain unchanged.\",\"reservation\":\"A5 can sound accusatory if performed harshly; sincerity works best as a wish for familiar connection.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S176-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"cb35339b8ebe0351d47688d8a1607c9fba06147f63e0ce9e878d5f09d56fdb27\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 collects a shift for a late-application exception; A3 explicitly says exceptions do not expire.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A3 answers B2's two-year objection, but A5's 'change of pace for us both' only loosely uses B4's one phone call.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 challenges elapsed time and B4 challenges proportionality, giving the presumed debt two credible objections.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 repeats the Saturday demand through a vague benefit rather than concretely redefining repayment.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes a late application and Saturday shift, though their shared workplace connection is only implied.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A3's exception-versus-favor distinction is sharp; A5's generic 'refreshing change of pace' weakens the close.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":77},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"I got your late job application accepted. You can take my Saturday shift.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"That was two years ago.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"And you've had the job for all of them. Saturday seems modest.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"It took you one phone call.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then make one to the manager. Tell her you're covering Saturday; we'll call that even.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"S176 turns a past exception A arranged into a still-unpaid obligation that casually authorizes present cooperation.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Ordinary reciprocal favors permit proportionate settlement; A treats exceptional access as continuing personal credit.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A3 refuses expiry, and revised A3 values two years of employment while A5 makes a nominally matching call carry the full shift obligation.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a converts a proportionality objection into a practical commitment at work; b negotiates an enthusiastic political endorsement after financial repayment.\",\"reason\":\"Original A5 weakl